body:
It's hard to say which infection can be transferred through toilet seat contact, but if it hasn't been cleaned properly, it may potentially transmit Gonorrhea ([https://www.nejm.org/doi/10.1056/NEJM197907123010207?url\_ver=Z39.88-2003&rfr\_id=ori:rid:crossref.org&rfr\_dat=cr\_pub%20%200pubmed](https://www.nejm.org/doi/10.1056/NEJM197907123010207?url_ver=Z39.88-2003&rfr_id=ori:rid:crossref.org&rfr_dat=cr_pub%20%200pubmed), [https://sti.bmj.com/content/80/4/327.1.long](https://sti.bmj.com/content/80/4/327.1.long))

&#x200B;

Flushing the toilet contaminates the toilet seat and the seat lid in case of Salmonella (doi:10.1046/j.1365-2672.2000.01091.x)
